  {
    "id": "debug-stuck",
    "title": "An enemy stuck behind a wall",
    "prompt": "The enemy moves straight toward its goal and stops at a wall. Repair find_path/findPath to search four neighbors and return a shortest path including start and goal. Coordinates are zero-based x/y; # is blocked. Visit neighbors in right, down, left, up order for reproducible ties. Return an empty path for unreachable or out-of-bounds endpoints and reject ragged grids. Inputs are borrowed and immutable. C writes into a caller-owned buffer: count is the path length, PATH_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL reports the required length without writing. C++ returns an owning vector. Zig returns an allocated slice that the caller frees, including empty results.",
    "hint": "Use a queue and record each cell's predecessor when first discovered. Reconstruct the path backward from the goal instead of walking straight through walls.",
    "lesson": "ai-pathing",
    "native": {
      "c": {
        "starter": "#include <assert.h>\n#include <stdbool.h>\n#include <stddef.h>\n#include <stdint.h>\n#include <limits.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\ntypedef struct { int x,y; } Point;\ntypedef enum { PATH_OK, PATH_INVALID_GRID, PATH_NO_MEMORY, PATH_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL } PathStatus;\n/* grid is immutable and borrowed. out/count belong to the caller.\n * On a short buffer, count receives the required length and out is untouched.\n * A valid but unreachable request succeeds with count zero. */\nPathStatus find_path(const char *const *grid,size_t rows,Point start,Point goal,Point *out,size_t capacity,size_t *count) {\n    *count=0;if(rows==0)return PATH_OK;\n    size_t columns=strlen(grid[0]);\n    if(start.x<0||start.y<0||goal.x<0||goal.y<0||(size_t)start.x>=columns||(size_t)goal.x>=columns||(size_t)start.y>=rows||(size_t)goal.y>=rows)return PATH_OK;\n    size_t length=(size_t)abs(goal.x-start.x)+1;\n    if(length>capacity||!out){*count=length;return PATH_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL;}\n    out[0]=start;size_t n=1;Point p=start;\n    while(p.x!=goal.x) {p.x+=p.x<goal.x?1:-1;if(grid[p.y][p.x]=='#')return PATH_OK;out[n++]=p;}\n    *count=n;return PATH_OK;\n}",
        "solution": "#include <assert.h>\n#include <stdbool.h>\n#include <stddef.h>\n#include <stdint.h>\n#include <limits.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\ntypedef struct { int x,y; } Point;\ntypedef enum { PATH_OK, PATH_INVALID_GRID, PATH_NO_MEMORY, PATH_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL } PathStatus;\n/* grid is immutable and borrowed. out/count belong to the caller.\n * On a short buffer, count receives the required length and out is untouched.\n * A valid but unreachable request succeeds with count zero. */\nPathStatus find_path(const char *const *grid,size_t rows,Point start,Point goal,Point *out,size_t capacity,size_t *count) {\n    *count=0;if(rows==0)return PATH_OK;\n    if(!grid||!grid[0]||rows>INT_MAX)return PATH_INVALID_GRID;\n    size_t columns=strlen(grid[0]);\n    if(columns>INT_MAX || (columns && rows>SIZE_MAX/columns))return PATH_INVALID_GRID;\n    for(size_t y=0;y<rows;y++)if(!grid[y]||strlen(grid[y])!=columns)return PATH_INVALID_GRID;\n    if(start.x<0||start.y<0||goal.x<0||goal.y<0||(size_t)start.x>=columns||(size_t)goal.x>=columns||(size_t)start.y>=rows||(size_t)goal.y>=rows)return PATH_OK;\n    if(grid[start.y][start.x]=='#'||grid[goal.y][goal.x]=='#')return PATH_OK;\n    size_t cells=rows*columns;if(cells>SIZE_MAX/sizeof(size_t))return PATH_INVALID_GRID;\n    size_t *previous=(size_t*)malloc(cells*sizeof(size_t));\n    size_t *queue=(size_t*)malloc(cells*sizeof(size_t));\n    if(!previous||!queue){free(previous);free(queue);return PATH_NO_MEMORY;}\n    for(size_t i=0;i<cells;i++)previous[i]=SIZE_MAX;\n    size_t first=(size_t)start.y*columns+(size_t)start.x,last=(size_t)goal.y*columns+(size_t)goal.x;\n    size_t head=0,tail=0;queue[tail++]=first;previous[first]=first;\n    const int dx[4]={1,0,-1,0},dy[4]={0,1,0,-1};\n    while(head<tail) {\n        size_t current=queue[head++];if(current==last)break;\n        int x=(int)(current%columns),y=(int)(current/columns);\n        for(int d=0;d<4;d++) {\n            int nx=x+dx[d],ny=y+dy[d];\n            if(nx<0||ny<0||(size_t)nx>=columns||(size_t)ny>=rows||grid[ny][nx]=='#')continue;\n            size_t next=(size_t)ny*columns+(size_t)nx;\n            if(previous[next]!=SIZE_MAX)continue;\n            previous[next]=current;queue[tail++]=next;\n        }\n    }\n    if(previous[last]==SIZE_MAX){free(queue);free(previous);return PATH_OK;}\n    size_t length=1;for(size_t node=last;node!=first;node=previous[node])length++;\n    *count=length;\n    if(length>capacity||!out){free(queue);free(previous);return PATH_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL;}\n    size_t node=last;for(size_t i=length;i>0;i--){out[i-1].x=(int)(node%columns);out[i-1].y=(int)(node/columns);node=previous[node];}\n    free(queue);free(previous);return PATH_OK;\n}\n",
        "tests": "static void check_path(const char *const *grid,size_t rows,Point start,Point goal,const Point *expected,size_t length) {Point out[64];size_t count=999;assert(find_path(grid,rows,start,goal,out,64,&count)==PATH_OK);assert(count==length);for(size_t i=0;i<count;i++)assert(out[i].x==expected[i].x&&out[i].y==expected[i].y);}int main(void) {\nconst char *grid0[]={\".#.\",\"...\"};const Point expected0[]={{0,0},{0,1},{1,1},{2,1},{2,0}};Point start0={0,0},goal0={2,0};check_path(grid0,2,start0,goal0,expected0,5);\nconst char *grid1[]={\"...\"};const Point expected1[]={{0,0},{1,0},{2,0}};Point start1={0,0},goal1={2,0};check_path(grid1,1,start1,goal1,expected1,3);\nconst char *grid2[]={\".#.\"};Point start2={0,0},goal2={2,0};check_path(grid2,1,start2,goal2,NULL,0);\nconst char *grid3[]={\".\",\".\",\".\"};const Point expected3[]={{0,0},{0,1},{0,2}};Point start3={0,0},goal3={0,2};check_path(grid3,3,start3,goal3,expected3,3);\nconst char *grid4[]={\"...\",\"...\"};const Point expected4[]={{0,0},{1,0},{1,1}};Point start4={0,0},goal4={1,1};check_path(grid4,2,start4,goal4,expected4,3);\nconst char *grid5[]={\"...\"};const Point expected5[]={{1,0}};Point start5={1,0},goal5={1,0};check_path(grid5,1,start5,goal5,expected5,1);\nconst char *grid6[]={\"#..\"};Point start6={0,0},goal6={2,0};check_path(grid6,1,start6,goal6,NULL,0);\nconst char *grid7[]={\"..#\"};Point start7={0,0},goal7={2,0};check_path(grid7,1,start7,goal7,NULL,0);\nPoint start8={0,0},goal8={0,0};check_path(NULL,0,start8,goal8,NULL,0);\nconst char *grid9[]={\"...\"};Point start9={-1,0},goal9={2,0};check_path(grid9,1,start9,goal9,NULL,0);\nconst char *grid10[]={\"...\"};Point start10={0,0},goal10={3,0};check_path(grid10,1,start10,goal10,NULL,0);\nconst char *grid11[]={\"...\",\"###\",\"...\"};Point start11={0,0},goal11={0,2};check_path(grid11,3,start11,goal11,NULL,0);\nconst char *ragged[]={\"..\",\"...\"};Point p={0,0},g={1,0},out[5]={{99,99},{99,99},{99,99},{99,99},{99,99}};size_t count=0;assert(find_path(ragged,2,p,g,out,5,&count)==PATH_INVALID_GRID);const char *wall[]={\".#.\",\"...\"};g.x=2;assert(find_path(wall,2,p,g,out,2,&count)==PATH_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL);assert(count==5&&out[0].x==99&&out[1].x==99);assert(find_path(wall,2,p,g,NULL,0,&count)==PATH_BUFFER_TOO_SMALL&&count==5);assert(strcmp(wall[0],\".#.\")==0);return 0;}"
      },
      "cpp": {
        "starter": "#include <cassert>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cstddef>\n#include <limits>\n#include <stdexcept>\n#include <string>\n#include <vector>\nstruct Point { int x,y; bool operator==(const Point&) const = default; };\n// grid is borrowed; the returned vector owns its points.\nstd::vector<Point> find_path(const std::vector<std::string>&grid,Point start,Point goal) {\n    if(grid.empty())return {};std::vector<Point> path{start};Point p=start;\n    while(p.x!=goal.x) {p.x+=p.x<goal.x?1:-1;if(p.x<0||p.y<0||static_cast<std::size_t>(p.y)>=grid.size()||static_cast<std::size_t>(p.x)>=grid[0].size()||grid[p.y][p.x]=='#')return {};path.push_back(p);}\n    return path;\n}",
        "solution": "#include <cassert>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cstddef>\n#include <limits>\n#include <stdexcept>\n#include <string>\n#include <vector>\nstruct Point { int x,y; bool operator==(const Point&) const = default; };\n// grid is borrowed; the returned vector owns its points.\nstd::vector<Point> find_path(const std::vector<std::string>&grid,Point start,Point goal) {\n    if(grid.empty())return {};\n    const auto rows=grid.size(),columns=grid.front().size();\n    if(rows>static_cast<std::size_t>(std::numeric_limits<int>::max())||columns>static_cast<std::size_t>(std::numeric_limits<int>::max())||(columns && rows>std::numeric_limits<std::size_t>::max()/columns))throw std::invalid_argument(\"invalid grid\");\n    for(const auto &row:grid)if(row.size()!=columns)throw std::invalid_argument(\"ragged grid\");\n    auto valid=[&](Point p){return p.x>=0&&p.y>=0&&static_cast<std::size_t>(p.x)<columns&&static_cast<std::size_t>(p.y)<rows&&grid[p.y][p.x]!='#';};\n    if(!valid(start)||!valid(goal))return {};\n    const auto unseen=std::numeric_limits<std::size_t>::max();\n    std::vector<std::size_t> previous(rows*columns,unseen),queue;\n    const auto first=static_cast<std::size_t>(start.y)*columns+start.x,last=static_cast<std::size_t>(goal.y)*columns+goal.x;\n    previous[first]=first;queue.push_back(first);\n    const Point directions[]={{1,0},{0,1},{-1,0},{0,-1}};\n    for(std::size_t head=0;head<queue.size();head++) {\n        const auto current=queue[head];if(current==last)break;\n        Point p{static_cast<int>(current%columns),static_cast<int>(current/columns)};\n        for(const auto d:directions) {\n            Point n{p.x+d.x,p.y+d.y};if(!valid(n))continue;\n            const auto next=static_cast<std::size_t>(n.y)*columns+n.x;\n            if(previous[next]!=unseen)continue;\n            previous[next]=current;queue.push_back(next);\n        }\n    }\n    if(previous[last]==unseen)return {};\n    std::vector<Point> path;\n    for(auto node=last;;node=previous[node]) {path.push_back({static_cast<int>(node%columns),static_cast<int>(node/columns)});if(node==first)break;}\n    std::reverse(path.begin(),path.end());return path;\n}\n",
        "tests": "int main() {\nassert(find_path({\".#.\",\"...\"},Point{0,0},Point{2,0})==std::vector<Point>({{0,0},{0,1},{1,1},{2,1},{2,0}}));\nassert(find_path({\"...\"},Point{0,0},Point{2,0})==std::vector<Point>({{0,0},{1,0},{2,0}}));\nassert(find_path({\".#.\"},Point{0,0},Point{2,0})==std::vector<Point>({}));\nassert(find_path({\".\",\".\",\".\"},Point{0,0},Point{0,2})==std::vector<Point>({{0,0},{0,1},{0,2}}));\nassert(find_path({\"...\",\"...\"},Point{0,0},Point{1,1})==std::vector<Point>({{0,0},{1,0},{1,1}}));\nassert(find_path({\"...\"},Point{1,0},Point{1,0})==std::vector<Point>({{1,0}}));\nassert(find_path({\"#..\"},Point{0,0},Point{2,0})==std::vector<Point>({}));\nassert(find_path({\"..#\"},Point{0,0},Point{2,0})==std::vector<Point>({}));\nassert(find_path({},Point{0,0},Point{0,0})==std::vector<Point>({}));\nassert(find_path({\"...\"},Point{-1,0},Point{2,0})==std::vector<Point>({}));\nassert(find_path({\"...\"},Point{0,0},Point{3,0})==std::vector<Point>({}));\nassert(find_path({\"...\",\"###\",\"...\"},Point{0,0},Point{0,2})==std::vector<Point>({}));\nbool rejected=false;try { (void)find_path({\"..\",\"...\"},{0,0},{1,0});}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){rejected=true;}assert(rejected);const std::vector<std::string> grid={\".#.\",\"...\"};(void)find_path(grid,{0,0},{2,0});assert(grid[0]==\".#.\");return 0;}"
      },
      "zig": {
        "starter": "const std = @import(\"std\");\nconst Point = struct { x: isize, y: isize };\n// grid is borrowed. The caller frees the returned slice with a, including empty results.\nfn findPath(a: std.mem.Allocator, grid: []const []const u8, start: Point, goal: Point) ![]Point {\n    if (grid.len == 0) return a.alloc(Point, 0);\n    var path = std.array_list.Managed(Point).init(a);\n    defer path.deinit();\n    try path.append(start);\n    var p = start;\n    while (p.x != goal.x) {\n        p.x += if (p.x < goal.x) @as(isize, 1) else -1;\n        if (p.x < 0 or p.y < 0 or p.y >= grid.len or p.x >= grid[0].len or grid[@intCast(p.y)][@intCast(p.x)] == '#') return a.alloc(Point, 0);\n        try path.append(p);\n    }\n    return path.toOwnedSlice();\n}\n",
        "solution": "const std = @import(\"std\");\nconst Point = struct { x: isize, y: isize };\n// grid is borrowed. The caller frees the returned slice with a, including empty results.\nfn findPath(a: std.mem.Allocator, grid: []const []const u8, start: Point, goal: Point) ![]Point {\n    if (grid.len == 0) return a.alloc(Point, 0);\n    const columns = grid[0].len;\n    for (grid) |row| {\n        if (row.len != columns) return error.InvalidGrid;\n    }\n    if (columns > std.math.maxInt(isize) or grid.len > std.math.maxInt(isize) or (columns != 0 and grid.len > std.math.maxInt(usize) / columns)) return error.InvalidGrid;\n    if (start.x < 0 or start.y < 0 or goal.x < 0 or goal.y < 0 or start.x >= columns or goal.x >= columns or start.y >= grid.len or goal.y >= grid.len) return a.alloc(Point, 0);\n    if (grid[@intCast(start.y)][@intCast(start.x)] == '#' or grid[@intCast(goal.y)][@intCast(goal.x)] == '#') return a.alloc(Point, 0);\n    const cells = grid.len * columns;\n    const previous = try a.alloc(usize, cells);\n    defer a.free(previous);\n    @memset(previous, std.math.maxInt(usize));\n    const queue = try a.alloc(usize, cells);\n    defer a.free(queue);\n    const first = @as(usize, @intCast(start.y)) * columns + @as(usize, @intCast(start.x));\n    const last = @as(usize, @intCast(goal.y)) * columns + @as(usize, @intCast(goal.x));\n    var head: usize = 0;\n    var tail: usize = 1;\n    queue[0] = first;\n    previous[first] = first;\n    const directions = [_]Point{ .{ .x = 1, .y = 0 }, .{ .x = 0, .y = 1 }, .{ .x = -1, .y = 0 }, .{ .x = 0, .y = -1 } };\n    while (head < tail) {\n        const current = queue[head];\n        head += 1;\n        if (current == last) break;\n        const x: @TypeOf(start.x) = @intCast(current % columns);\n        const y: @TypeOf(start.y) = @intCast(current / columns);\n        for (directions) |d| {\n            const nx = x + d.x;\n            const ny = y + d.y;\n            if (nx < 0 or ny < 0 or nx >= columns or ny >= grid.len or grid[@intCast(ny)][@intCast(nx)] == '#') continue;\n            const next = @as(usize, @intCast(ny)) * columns + @as(usize, @intCast(nx));\n            if (previous[next] != std.math.maxInt(usize)) continue;\n            previous[next] = current;\n            queue[tail] = next;\n            tail += 1;\n        }\n    }\n    if (previous[last] == std.math.maxInt(usize)) return a.alloc(Point, 0);\n    var length: usize = 1;\n    var node = last;\n    while (node != first) {\n        length += 1;\n        node = previous[node];\n    }\n    const path = try a.alloc(Point, length);\n    node = last;\n    var i = length;\n    while (i > 0) {\n        i -= 1;\n        path[i] = .{ .x = @intCast(node % columns), .y = @intCast(node / columns) };\n        node = previous[node];\n    }\n    return path;\n}\n",
        "tests": "fn checkPath(grid: []const []const u8, start: Point, goal: Point, expected: []const Point) !void {\n    const path = try findPath(std.testing.allocator, grid, start, goal);\n    defer std.testing.allocator.free(path);\n    try std.testing.expectEqualDeep(expected, path);\n}\ntest \"find shortest four-neighbor routes\" {\n    try checkPath(&.{ \".#.\", \"...\" }, .{ .x = 0, .y = 0 }, .{ .x = 2, .y = 0 }, &.{ .{ .x = 0, .y = 0 }, .{ .x = 0, .y = 1 }, .{ .x = 1, .y = 1 }, .{ .x = 2, .y = 1 }, .{ .x = 2, .y = 0 } });\n    try checkPath(&.{\"...\"}, .{ .x = 0, .y = 0 }, .{ .x = 2, .y = 0 }, &.{ .{ .x = 0, .y = 0 }, .{ .x = 1, .y = 0 }, .{ .x = 2, .y = 0 } });\n    try checkPath(&.{\".#.\"}, .{ .x = 0, .y = 0 }, .{ .x = 2, .y = 0 }, &.{});\n    try checkPath(&.{ \".\", \".\", \".\" }, .{ .x = 0, .y = 0 }, .{ .x = 0, .y = 2 }, &.{ .{ .x = 0, .y = 0 }, .{ .x = 0, .y = 1 }, .{ .x = 0, .y = 2 } });\n    try checkPath(&.{ \"...\", \"...\" }, .{ .x = 0, .y = 0 }, .{ .x = 1, .y = 1 }, &.{ .{ .x = 0, .y = 0 }, .{ .x = 1, .y = 0 }, .{ .x = 1, .y = 1 } });\n    try checkPath(&.{\"...\"}, .{ .x = 1, .y = 0 }, .{ .x = 1, .y = 0 }, &.{.{ .x = 1, .y = 0 }});\n    try checkPath(&.{\"#..\"}, .{ .x = 0, .y = 0 }, .{ .x = 2, .y = 0 }, &.{});\n    try checkPath(&.{\"..#\"}, .{ .x = 0, .y = 0 }, .{ .x = 2, .y = 0 }, &.{});\n    try checkPath(&.{}, .{ .x = 0, .y = 0 }, .{ .x = 0, .y = 0 }, &.{});\n    try checkPath(&.{\"...\"}, .{ .x = -1, .y = 0 }, .{ .x = 2, .y = 0 }, &.{});\n    try checkPath(&.{\"...\"}, .{ .x = 0, .y = 0 }, .{ .x = 3, .y = 0 }, &.{});\n    try checkPath(&.{ \"...\", \"###\", \"...\" }, .{ .x = 0, .y = 0 }, .{ .x = 0, .y = 2 }, &.{});\n    try std.testing.expectError(error.InvalidGrid, findPath(std.testing.allocator, &.{ \"..\", \"...\" }, .{ .x = 0, .y = 0 }, .{ .x = 1, .y = 0 }));\n}\n"
      }
    }
  }
